invariant: INV-14
file: src/pbkdf2.c
catches: scram_test
reason: pbkdf2_hmac_sha256 counts its blocks from 0. RFC 8018 section 5.2
  counts them from 1, so every key the call derives is another key: a
  SCRAM verifier made here matches no other implementation's, and a login
  against a verifier that PostgreSQL made fails. The call still returns
  CH_OK and fills its output. bin/scram_test holds the key to RFC 7914's
  vectors and to RFC 7677's exchange.

--- old
    uint32_t block_index = 1;
--- new
    uint32_t block_index = 0;
